    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22209" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-artĭfĭcĭālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>inartificial</i>, <i>not
				according to the rules of art</i> (post-Aug.): illas
			(probationes) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτέχνους,</span> id est
			inartificiales; has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντέχνους,</span> id
			est artificiales vocaverunt, <i><span class="en">Quint. 5, 1,
				1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">probationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 5,
					5, 2</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 5, 10, 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argumenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 5, § 474</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">§ 557</span></i>; <i><span class="en">§
				560</span></i>.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnartĭfĭ-cĭālĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>inartificially</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se gerere (opp. artificialiter),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 17, 42</span></i>
			.</div>
